# agent-audit allowlist: copy to ~/.claude-audit/allow (or $CLAUDE_AUDIT_DIR/allow).
#
# One glob per line, matched against a session's working directory (cwd).
# `*` also matches `/`, and a leading `~` is your home folder. Lines starting
# with `#` and blank lines are ignored. No file means no allowlist.
#
# A SECRET-EXPOSED finding from a matching session still appears in the report,
# under "Secrets exposed in allowlisted sessions", but it doesn't make the run
# FLAGGED and doesn't alert. The model's own FLAGGED or CRITICAL verdict on that
# session still alerts.
#
# List only sessions that plant fake secrets on purpose, such as redaction tests.
# A glob that is too broad hides real leaks.
#
# Examples:
# ~/dev/*/my-redaction-lib/.claude/worktrees/*
# /home/me/dev/private/ai-dev/.claude/worktrees/agent-audit
